{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_001","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":".. DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE!!!\n.. Generated automatically from Godot engine sources.\n.. Generator: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/doc/tools/make_rst.py.\n.. XML source: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/doc/classes/JSON.xml.","location_hint":"paragraph 2","char_start":19,"char_end":272,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_002","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"**Inherits:** :ref:`Resource<class_Resource>` **<** :ref:`RefCounted<class_RefCounted>` **<** :ref:`Object<class_Object>`","location_hint":"paragraph 5","char_start":302,"char_end":423,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_003","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Helper class for creating and parsing JSON data.","location_hint":"paragraph 6","char_start":425,"char_end":473,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_004","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":".. rst-class:: classref-introduction-group","location_hint":"paragraph 7","char_start":475,"char_end":517,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_005","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"The **JSON** class enables all data types to be converted to and from a JSON string. This is useful for serializing data, e.g. to save to a file or send over the network.","location_hint":"paragraph 9","char_start":544,"char_end":714,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_006","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ :ref:`stringify()<class_JSON_method_stringify>` is used to convert any data type into a JSON string.","location_hint":"paragraph 10","char_start":716,"char_end":818,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_007","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ :ref:`parse()<class_JSON_method_parse>` is used to convert any existing JSON data into a :ref:`Variant<class_Variant>` that can be used within Godot. If successfully parsed, use :ref:`data<class_JSON_property_data>` to retrieve the :ref:`Variant<class_Variant>`, and use :ref:`@GlobalScope.typeof()<class_@GlobalScope_method_typeof>` to check if the Variant's type is what you expect. JSON Objects are converted into a :ref:`Dictionary<class_Dictionary>`, but JSON data can be used to store :ref:`Array<class_Array>`\\ s, numbers, :ref:`String<class_String>`\\ s and even just a boolean.","location_hint":"paragraph 11","char_start":820,"char_end":1407,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_008","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"var data_to_send = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n var json_string = JSON.stringify(data_to_send)\n # Save data\n # ...\n # Retrieve data\n var json = JSON.new()\n var error = json.parse(json_string)\n if error == OK:\n var data_received = json.data\n if typeof(data_received) == TYPE_ARRAY:\n print(data_received) # Prints the array.\n else:\n print(\"Unexpected data\")\n else:\n print(\"JSON Parse Error: \", json.get_error_message(), \" in \", json_string, \" at line \", json.get_error_line())","location_hint":"paragraph 13","char_start":1414,"char_end":1876,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_009","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Alternatively, you can parse strings using the static :ref:`parse_string()<class_JSON_method_parse_string>` method, but it doesn't handle errors.","location_hint":"paragraph 14","char_start":1878,"char_end":2023,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_010","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"var data = JSON.parse_string(json_string) # Returns null if parsing failed.","location_hint":"paragraph 16","char_start":2030,"char_end":2105,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_011","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ **Note:** Both parse methods do not fully comply with the JSON specification:","location_hint":"paragraph 17","char_start":2107,"char_end":2186,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_012","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"- Trailing commas in arrays or objects are ignored, instead of causing a parser error.","location_hint":"paragraph 18","char_start":2188,"char_end":2274,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_013","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"- New line and tab characters are accepted in string literals, and are treated like their corresponding escape sequences ``\\n`` and ``\\t``.","location_hint":"paragraph 19","char_start":2276,"char_end":2415,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_014","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"- Numbers are parsed using :ref:`String.to_float()<class_String_method_to_float>` which is generally more lax than the JSON specification.","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":2417,"char_end":2555,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_015","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"- Certain errors, such as invalid Unicode sequences, do not cause a parser error. Instead, the string is cleaned up and an error is logged to the console.","location_hint":"paragraph 21","char_start":2557,"char_end":2711,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
