{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_056","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Attempts to parse the ``json_text`` provided.","location_hint":"paragraph 75","char_start":9574,"char_end":9619,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_057","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Returns an :ref:`Error<enum_@GlobalScope_Error>`. If the parse was successful, it returns :ref:`@GlobalScope.OK<class_@GlobalScope_constant_OK>` and the result can be retrieved using :ref:`data<class_JSON_property_data>`. If unsuccessful, use :ref:`get_error_line()<class_JSON_method_get_error_line>` and :ref:`get_error_message()<class_JSON_method_get_error_message>` to identify the source of the failure.","location_hint":"paragraph 76","char_start":9621,"char_end":10028,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_058","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Non-static variant of :ref:`parse_string()<class_JSON_method_parse_string>`, if you want custom error handling.","location_hint":"paragraph 77","char_start":10030,"char_end":10141,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_059","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"The optional ``keep_text`` argument instructs the parser to keep a copy of the original text. This text can be obtained later by using the :ref:`get_parsed_text()<class_JSON_method_get_parsed_text>` function and is used when saving the resource (instead of generating new text from :ref:`data<class_JSON_property_data>`).","location_hint":"paragraph 78","char_start":10143,"char_end":10464,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
