{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_067","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":".. rst-class:: classref-method","location_hint":"paragraph 88","char_start":10920,"char_end":10950,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_068","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":":ref:`String<class_String>` **stringify**\\ (\\ data\\: :ref:`Variant<class_Variant>`, indent\\: :ref:`String<class_String>` = \"\", sort_keys\\: :ref:`bool<class_bool>` = true, full_precision\\: :ref:`bool<class_bool>` = false\\ ) |static| :ref:`🔗<class_JSON_method_stringify>`","location_hint":"paragraph 89","char_start":10952,"char_end":11222,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_069","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Converts a :ref:`Variant<class_Variant>` var to JSON text and returns the result. Useful for serializing data to store or send over the network.","location_hint":"paragraph 90","char_start":11224,"char_end":11368,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_070","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ **Note:** The JSON specification does not define integer or float types, but only a *number* type. Therefore, converting a Variant to JSON text will convert all numerical values to :ref:`float<class_float>` types.","location_hint":"paragraph 91","char_start":11370,"char_end":11585,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_071","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ **Note:** If ``full_precision`` is ``true``, when stringifying floats, the unreliable digits are stringified in addition to the reliable digits to guarantee exact decoding.","location_hint":"paragraph 92","char_start":11587,"char_end":11761,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_072","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"The ``indent`` parameter controls if and how something is indented; its contents will be used where there should be an indent in the output. Even spaces like ``\" \"`` will work. ``\\t`` and ``\\n`` can also be used for a tab indent, or to make a newline for each indent respectively.","location_hint":"paragraph 93","char_start":11763,"char_end":12043,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_073","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"\\ **Warning:** Non-finite numbers are not supported in JSON. Any occurrences of :ref:`@GDScript.INF<class_@GDScript_constant_INF>` will be replaced with ``1e99999``, and negative :ref:`@GDScript.INF<class_@GDScript_constant_INF>` will be replaced with ``-1e99999``, but they will be interpreted correctly as infinity by most JSON parsers. :ref:`@GDScript.NAN<class_@GDScript_constant_NAN>` will be replaced with ``null``, and it will not be interpreted as NaN in JSON parsers. If you expect non-finite numbers, consider passing your data through :ref:`from_native()<class_JSON_method_from_native>` first.","location_hint":"paragraph 94","char_start":12045,"char_end":12649,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_074","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"## JSON.stringify(my_dictionary)\n {\"name\":\"my_dictionary\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"entities\":[{\"name\":\"entity_0\",\"value\":\"value_0\"},{\"name\":\"entity_1\",\"value\":\"value_1\"}]}","location_hint":"paragraph 97","char_start":12681,"char_end":12846,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_075","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"## JSON.stringify(my_dictionary, \"\\t\")\n {\n \"name\": \"my_dictionary\",\n \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n \"entities\": [\n {\n \"name\": \"entity_0\",\n \"value\": \"value_0\"\n },\n {\n \"name\": \"entity_1\",\n \"value\": \"value_1\"\n }\n ]\n }","location_hint":"paragraph 98","char_start":12849,"char_end":13053,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_076","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"## JSON.stringify(my_dictionary, \"...\")\n {\n ...\"name\": \"my_dictionary\",\n ...\"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n ...\"entities\": [\n ......{\n .........\"name\": \"entity_0\",\n .........\"value\": \"value_0\"\n ......},\n ......{\n .........\"name\": \"entity_1\",\n .........\"value\": \"value_1\"\n ......}\n ...]\n }","location_hint":"paragraph 99","char_start":13056,"char_end":13333,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_077","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":".. rst-class:: classref-item-separator","location_hint":"paragraph 100","char_start":13335,"char_end":13373,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
