{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_080","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":":ref:`Variant<class_Variant>` **to_native**\\ (\\ json\\: :ref:`Variant<class_Variant>`, allow_objects\\: :ref:`bool<class_bool>` = false\\ ) |static| :ref:`🔗<class_JSON_method_to_native>`","location_hint":"paragraph 104","char_start":13447,"char_end":13631,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_081","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"Converts a JSON-compliant value that was created with :ref:`from_native()<class_JSON_method_from_native>` back to native engine types.","location_hint":"paragraph 105","char_start":13633,"char_end":13767,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_082","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"By default, objects are ignored for security reasons, unless ``allow_objects`` is ``true``.","location_hint":"paragraph 106","char_start":13769,"char_end":13860,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_083","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"You can convert a JSON string back to a native value like this:","location_hint":"paragraph 107","char_start":13862,"char_end":13925,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_084","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"func decode_data(string, allow_objects = false):\n return JSON.to_native(JSON.parse_string(string), allow_objects)","location_hint":"paragraph 109","char_start":13932,"char_end":14045,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_085","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":".. |virtual| replace:: :abbr:`virtual (This method should typically be overridden by the user to have any effect.)`\n.. |required| replace:: :abbr:`required (This method is required to be overridden when extending its base class.)`\n.. |const| replace:: :abbr:`const (This method has no side effects.","location_hint":"paragraph 110","char_start":14047,"char_end":14345,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a6a330af5a09_086","source_id":"src_a6a330af5a09","source_hash":"86077c49cf7475e767f1a0213d3c6cad4da39f2b7d1de69829f6d0432f232260","text":"It doesn't modify any of the instance's member variables.)`\n.. |vararg| replace:: :abbr:`vararg (This method accepts any number of arguments after the ones described here.)`\n.. |constructor| replace:: :abbr:`constructor (This method is used to construct a type.)`\n.. |static| replace:: :abbr:`static (This method doesn't need an instance to be called, so it can be called directly using the class name.)`\n.. |operator| replace:: :abbr:`operator (This method describes a valid operator to use with this type as left-hand operand.)`\n.. |bitfield| replace:: :abbr:`BitField (This value is an integer composed as a bitmask of the following flags.)`\n.. |void| replace:: :abbr:`void (No return value.)`","location_hint":"paragraph 110","char_start":14346,"char_end":15042,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T04:13:11.979Z"}
